{:id :EACL-FORMAL-007
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "secure-format/cljs-hostile-edn"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions ["current worktree at discovery"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "The portable decoder rethrew every CLJS ExceptionInfo on the assumption that it came from EACL validation. cljs.reader uses ExceptionInfo for duplicate-key and unknown-tag parse failures, so those failures escaped without the required typed EACL malformed-format error. JVM reader exceptions took the generic catch path and were normalized correctly."
 :fix
 "The decoder now rethrows only ExceptionInfo values already carrying the EACL format-error type and normalizes every host-reader ExceptionInfo to the typed malformed error."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.secure-format-test/canonical-portable-format-test (CLJ and CLJS)"
  "full DataScript CLJS suite: 47 tests, 283 assertions"]}
